{{also|Tongue}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|tounge}} (''obsolete, now considered a misspelling''); [[tung]] (''obsolete or informal/eye dialect''); [[tong]], [[tonge]], [[toong]], [[toongue]], [[toung]], [[toungue]], [[tunge]] (''all obsolete'')

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|tonge|id=tongue}}, {{m|enm|tunge}}, {{m|enm|tung}}, from {{inh|en|ang|tunge}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*tungā}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*tungǭ||tongue}} (compare {{cog|fy|tonge}}, {{cog|nl|tong}}, {{cog|lb|Zong}}, {{cog|zza|Zon}}, {{cog|de|Zunge}}, {{cog|yi|צונג}}, {{cog|da|tunge}}, {{cog|nb|tunge}}, {{cog|sv|tunga}}, {{cog|got|𐍄𐌿𐌲𐌲𐍉}}), from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*dn̥ǵʰwéh₂s}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sga|tengae}}, {{cog|la|lingua}}, {{cog|xto|käntu}}, {{cog|txb|kantwo}}, {{cog|lt|liežùvis}}, {{cog|ru|язык}}, {{cog|pl|język}}, {{cog|xcl|լեզու}}, {{cog|ae|𐬵𐬌𐬰𐬎𐬎𐬁}}, {{cog|ask|žū}}, {{cog|bsh|dić}}, {{cog|sa|जिह्वा|tr=jihvā́}}. {{doublet|en|language|lingua}}.

