===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|music|ambitransitive}} On a [[wind]] instrument, to [[articulate]] a [[note]] by starting the air with a tap of the tongue, as though by speaking a 'd' or 't' sound ([[alveolar]] [[plosive]]).
#: {{ux|en|Playing wind instruments involves '''tonguing''' on the reed or mouthpiece.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} To manipulate with the tongue, as in [[kiss]]ing or [[oral sex]].
#* {{RQ:Joyce Ulysses|chapter=8|passage=Hot I '''tongued''' her. She kissed me. I was kissed. All yielding she tossed my hair. Kissed, she kissed me. }}
# To [[protrude]] in relatively long, narrow sections.
#: {{ux|en|a soil horizon that '''tongues''' into clay}}
# To join by means of a [[tongue and groove]].
#: {{ux|en|to '''tongue''' boards together}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|obsolete}} To [[talk]]; to [[prate]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To speak; to utter.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Cymbeline|V|4|text=’Tis still a dream, or else such stuff as madmen<br>'''Tongue''' and brain not;}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To chide; to scold.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Measure|IV|4|text=How might she '''tongue''' me!}}

